│ Reasoning:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is that the current code incorrectly handles two-digit   │
│ years in RFC850 date parsing. It assumes that years 0-69 are in    │
│ the 2000s and 70-99 are in the 1970s-1990s, which is not aligned   │
│ with RFC 7231's requirement. The correct behavior is to compare    │
│ the year with the current year and interpret a future two-digit    │
│ year as the most recent year in the past with the same last two    │
│ digits. The provided code context already includes the necessary   │
│ logic for parsing the date, so the fix lies within the year        │
│ calculation. We need to remove the hardcoded ranges and instead    │
│ compare the year with the current year.                            │
│                                                                    │
│ Patch:                                                             │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
